  "documentation": {
    "range": "This species is distributed in the Indo-Pacific from South Africa and Madagascar, western Mascarenes&#160;to the Red Sea, the Persian/Arabian Gulf and Sri Lanka. In the Pacific, it occurs from Korea and southern Japan,&#160;the&#160;Ogasawara Islands, Taiwan, Indonesia, the Philippines, the&#160;Arafura Sea, Australia (Shark Bay, Western Australia north and east to Sydney, New South Wales) to New Caledonia, Vanuatu and northern New Zealand (Masuda&#160;<em>et al.</em>&#160;1984,&#160;<span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">Smith 1986,&#160;</span>Paulin&#160;<em>et al.</em>&#160;1989, Russell and Houston 1989, Randall 1995, Larson&#160;<em>et al.&#160;</em>2013, J. Bishop and M. Al-Husaini pers. comm. 2014, Jawad&#160;<em>et al.&#160;</em>2014, iDigBio database accessed April 2019). Adults occupy depths between 20-200 metres, and juveniles occasionally occur shallower (Paxton 1984).",
    "population": "Population data are limited. There are about 200 museum records of this species in the iDigBio database (accessed April 2019).",
    "habitats": "This demersal species inhabits coral and rocky reefs (Lieske and Myers 1994). The maximum total length is 30 cm (Nagamatsu 2009), though it is more commonly found to 17 cm (Paxton 1984).",
    "threats": "There are no known major threats.",
    "measures": "There are no species-specific conservation measures.",
    "use_trade": "This species is not targeted, but has been taken as bycatch in bottom trawl fisheries in parts of its range, including the East China Sea (Nagamatsu 2009, Kim <em>et al. </em>2010) and Western Australia (Newman <em>et al. </em>2000). It is also a very minor component of trade in saltwater aquaria (J. Moore pers. comm. 2019).",
    "rationale": "This widely distributed, reef-associated species has no known major threats; therefore, it is listed as Least Concern.",
    "trend_justification": null,
    "taxonomic_notes": null
  },
